> rop fa
rop fa: fa = d + s, applied once per fragment (s what a fragment brings, d the cell's value)
  order: as real functions the result does not depend on the order of the fragments (both orders expand to the same rational function); in f32 each operation rounds, so it does unless every step is exact
  fixed-function states that compute it (each a proposal: the pipeline changes):
  blending: VK_BLEND_OP_ADD, source factor ONE, destination factor ONE on a float target (R32_SFLOAT): s + d
      fa and s + d expand to the same polynomial; one f32 operation: exact if the blender rounds it to nearest (Vulkan asks for the target's precision, not the rounding: to measure)
      price: rop_blend 2 a fragment under fixed, against 138.75 (one global float atomic add, atomic_global_f): cheaper
      pipeline: VkPipelineColorBlendAttachmentState: blendEnable, colorBlendOp = VK_BLEND_OP_ADD, srcColorBlendFactor = VK_BLEND_FACTOR_ONE, dstColorBlendFactor = VK_BLEND_FACTOR_ONE; an R32_SFLOAT colour attachment; one point per contribution, its position the cell, its colour s
  not in any price: the draw's setup (a render pass, the pipeline, one vertex per contribution) and reading the target back
> rop kb
rop kb: kb = d + s*k, applied once per fragment (s what a fragment brings, d the cell's value, k a pipeline constant)
  order: as real functions the result does not depend on the order of the fragments (both orders expand to the same rational function); in f32 each operation rounds, so it does unless every step is exact
  fixed-function states that compute it (each a proposal: the pipeline changes):
  blending: VK_BLEND_OP_ADD, source factor CONSTANT_COLOR, destination factor ONE on a float target (R32_SFLOAT): s*k + d
      kb and s*k + d expand to the same polynomial; the blender does 2 operations whose rounding Vulkan does not fix (it may fuse the multiply and the add): equal as real functions, bit for bit only where every step is exact
      price: rop_blend 2 a fragment under fixed, against 144.5 (a global compare-and-swap around the update: atomic_global_cas 143.5 + 1): cheaper
      pipeline: VkPipelineColorBlendAttachmentState: blendEnable, colorBlendOp = VK_BLEND_OP_ADD, srcColorBlendFactor = VK_BLEND_FACTOR_CONSTANT_COLOR, dstColorBlendFactor = VK_BLEND_FACTOR_ONE, blendConstants = k; an R32_SFLOAT colour attachment; one point per contribution, its position the cell, its colour s
  not in any price: the draw's setup (a render pass, the pipeline, one vertex per contribution) and reading the target back
